WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.350
I'm here at the Lucasfilm compound

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.000
at the Presidio in San Francisco.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.807
This is a place where
they literally manufacture

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:09.120
magic and wonder.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.430
As you can see there's a
statue of Yoda right here.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.630
Yoda is 900 years old.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.543
So as you can see, he has
a bladder control problem.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.813
Pee, I must.

00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:24.587
(Star Wars orchestral music)

00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:27.587
(audience cheering)

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:31.470
This is John Singh.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.500
Hi John, how are you?

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.333
Hi, nice to meet you.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.470
And you work here at Lucasfilm?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:35.303
I do, welcome.

00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:39.240
Here, we have some of the
original costumes from the movies.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.073
This is incredible.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:43.150
Now this, I don't know
a lot about Star Wars.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.212
This is Darth Vader, is that correct?

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.280
This is Darth Vader, yes.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.347
Looks like there's a
retractable door here.

00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:51.940
(audience laughing)

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.477
It does look like that, yeah.

00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:54.310
You can just push,

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.143
I think it's this button and then

00:00:55.143 --> 00:00:56.407
(imitating mechanical whirring)

00:00:56.407 --> 00:00:58.157
(loud exhaling whoosh)

00:00:58.157 --> 00:00:59.399
Yes, much better.

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:00.886
This is Jordan Schlansky.

00:01:00.886 --> 00:01:02.356
Hi.
He's a producer on our show.

00:01:02.356 --> 00:01:03.189
Hi, Jordan.
It's a pleasure.

00:01:03.189 --> 00:01:04.022
How are you?
Good to see you.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:06.230
Jordan is our resident Star Wars expert.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.250
Is that fair to say, Jordan?

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.083
Yes, sir.

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:08.916
Jordan, you have some problems

00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:10.870
with this Darth Vader costume?

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.703
Well, I just noticed that John had said

00:01:11.703 --> 00:01:12.940
that it was an original

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.610
and then I also noticed
that the chest plate

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.020
doesn't have the Hebrew lettering

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.000
in these three areas
that the original has,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.980
which led me to believe that
maybe it actually is a replica.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.400
It probably is.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.233
I see.

00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:26.295
So earlier, when you said you
think this is the original,

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:27.629
you were lying to me.

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.441
I was misinformed.

00:01:29.441 --> 00:01:31.433
[Male Voiceover] Liar.

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:32.550
There's Darth Maul's lightsaber,

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.490
a double-bladed lightsaber.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.710
And Darth Maul actually
specializes in musical theater.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.350
Is that right?

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:40.613
I'm gonna wow ya!

00:01:41.613 --> 00:01:43.970
This is, he's a bounty
hunter, I think I know that.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.320
Yeah, very good, yeah.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.091
And he has some braids from Jedi.

00:01:47.091 --> 00:01:48.431
Oh, what's that all about?
What is that?

00:01:48.431 --> 00:01:50.750
Yeah, these are the braids
from the Jedi that he's killed.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.158
Jordan, do you know any inaccuracies

00:01:52.158 --> 00:01:54.400
with the Boba Fett costume?

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.869
Well, John, the one thing
that you mentioned that,

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:59.480
again I question, was you
would call these Jedi braids.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.710
I'd always heard of them
referred to as Wookiee braids.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:03.987
[Male Voiceover] Liar.

00:02:03.987 --> 00:02:05.565
This is one of the
operations that was used

00:02:05.565 --> 00:02:07.950
in a shot for his chest.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.220
Has he heard of Nivea cream?

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.331
Look at his arm.

00:02:10.331 --> 00:02:12.380
For four million light-years,
it's a long trip.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.047
Okay, you just said four
million light-years.

00:02:14.047 --> 00:02:14.880
Yep.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.015
Jordan, would you step in please?

00:02:16.015 --> 00:02:16.848
How you doing?

00:02:16.848 --> 00:02:17.681
Yeah, what is it?

00:02:17.681 --> 00:02:19.160
It's actually six million light-years

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.448
from home E.T. traveled.

00:02:20.448 --> 00:02:21.787
[Male Voiceover] Sad.

00:02:21.787 --> 00:02:23.510
(audience laughing)

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.510
The original models and props,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.970
even though this is from Dragon Slayer.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:27.803
One of the other cool things we have

00:02:27.803 --> 00:02:31.122
is one of the original whips
used from Indiana Jones.

00:02:31.122 --> 00:02:32.688
(suspenseful music)

00:02:32.688 --> 00:02:34.620
(whip cracking)

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.453
Do you mind if I,

00:02:35.453 --> 00:02:36.380
is it okay if I--
Sure, go ahead.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.710
Yeah, look it.
Oh, wow.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.503
Look at that.

00:02:39.503 --> 00:02:40.336
(whip cracking)

00:02:40.336 --> 00:02:41.652
Whoa, did you hear that?

00:02:41.652 --> 00:02:42.935
Look at that.

00:02:42.935 --> 00:02:43.768
(whip cracking)

00:02:43.768 --> 00:02:46.890
Ow, I just whipped myself in the back.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.557
One of the original Imperial Walkers.

00:02:48.557 --> 00:02:49.390
Oh, cool.
Yeah.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.223
These are so cool.
Yeah.

00:02:50.223 --> 00:02:51.056
Look at that.

00:02:51.056 --> 00:02:52.620
I remember those walk.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.580
Yeah, from The Empire Strikes Back.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.413
Yeah.

00:02:54.413 --> 00:02:55.898
(lasers shooting)

00:02:55.898 --> 00:02:57.260
(jet whooshing)

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.412
I love the way these things
were sort of just like--

00:02:58.412 --> 00:02:59.245
Yeah.

00:03:00.269 --> 00:03:02.560
(audience jeering)

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.393
I think this goes here.

00:03:03.393 --> 00:03:05.010
No, you have the wrong one.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.850
Problem is this part needs to go in here

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.046
to get that tab in.

00:03:08.046 --> 00:03:12.506
I don't get this.

00:03:12.506 --> 00:03:14.173
Pretty much there.

00:03:15.215 --> 00:03:18.873
(audience laughing)

00:03:18.873 --> 00:03:19.870
This is Industrial Light &amp; Magic.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.036
This is Industrial Light &amp; Magic.

00:03:21.036 --> 00:03:24.512
They're pretty much the
biggest visual effects company

00:03:24.512 --> 00:03:26.550
in the entertainment industry.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:27.641
You mind if we come in for a sec?

00:03:27.641 --> 00:03:28.970
No, don't mind at all.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.430
This is our nerd corner here.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.263
Nerd corner.

00:03:32.263 --> 00:03:33.096
That's what we call it.

00:03:33.096 --> 00:03:33.929
You said it, I didn't.

00:03:33.929 --> 00:03:34.762
Hi, what is your name?

00:03:34.762 --> 00:03:35.595
My name's Charles.

00:03:35.595 --> 00:03:36.428
Hey Charles, really good to meet you.

00:03:36.428 --> 00:03:37.560
What is this fan for?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:38.393
This is,

00:03:38.393 --> 00:03:40.569
this is so you never have to go outside

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:41.895
to experience a cool breeze.
That's right.

00:03:41.895 --> 00:03:44.400
It simulates an outdoor experience.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.390
Simulates what it will be like

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.910
if you took 10 steps and walked outside.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:48.743
Absolutely.

00:03:48.743 --> 00:03:49.600
Kevin, is that correct?
Kevin, yeah you're right.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.590
I want to ask you quickly

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.680
about your professional wrestling figures.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:53.513
Okay, yeah.
What's that all about?

00:03:53.513 --> 00:03:55.892
Basically, my folks just wanted them

00:03:55.892 --> 00:03:57.237
to get out of the house.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.380
[Kevin] Big John Studd.
[Conan] Yes.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.340
[Kevin] King Kong Bundy.
[Conan] Yes.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.320
And I was like, I'll take these.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.909
I know exactly where they'll fit in great.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.805
Were they worried that
you have a vast collection

00:04:04.805 --> 00:04:06.141
of men without shirts?

00:04:06.141 --> 00:04:07.880
(audience laughing)

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:08.713
This is Maia, is that right?

00:04:08.713 --> 00:04:09.546
Maia?
Yes, Maia.

00:04:09.546 --> 00:04:10.379
Which, Maia?

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:11.212
Kayser.

00:04:11.212 --> 00:04:12.045
Maia Kayser.

00:04:12.045 --> 00:04:12.878
Yeah.
Let me ask you something.

00:04:12.878 --> 00:04:15.231
What is the male to female ratio here?

00:04:15.231 --> 00:04:18.519
I've walked around, the
ratio is I think 800 to 1.

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:21.531
(audience laughing)

00:04:21.531 --> 00:04:23.310
I just wanted you to meet my friend.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.167
This is my friend Charles.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:25.049
Hey.
Hey.

00:04:25.049 --> 00:04:25.970
I thought you two should meet.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:26.803
Hey.
Hi.

00:04:26.803 --> 00:04:27.860
Hi.
How're you doing?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:30.610
(romantic music)

00:04:32.673 --> 00:04:34.360
This is Mike Sanders, is that right?

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.193
That's correct.

00:04:35.193 --> 00:04:37.960
What we're gonna do is turn
this place into a virtual studio

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.890
and they're gonna alter the performance

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:41.130
of some digital creatures.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.220
And to do that I need
to get into a special...

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.540
It's a

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.670
humbling lycra suit.

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:48.124
Why you say humbling?

00:04:48.124 --> 00:04:49.574
Well, we're gonna find out.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.633
Perfect.

00:04:51.633 --> 00:04:55.079
(dramatic trombone music)

00:04:59.946 --> 00:05:01.529
This was a mistake.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.790
We're gonna plug you right into

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.470
the first digital
character we've got here.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.517
It's a demo character we call The Schwa.

00:05:08.517 --> 00:05:09.676
The Schwa.
The Schwa.

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:11.183
Oh, here he is.
Yep.

00:05:11.183 --> 00:05:13.253
This is The Schwa right here.

00:05:13.253 --> 00:05:14.889
So I am now The Schwa.

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:16.800
[Mike] Yep, exactly.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.551
Is The Schwa been in any Star Wars movies?

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:20.890
No.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:24.200
Okay, this is where The
Schwa gets the phone call

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.040
that he's not good enough for Star Wars.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.662
He's been cut.

00:05:27.662 --> 00:05:30.332
(disguising voice) Wha- what?

00:05:30.332 --> 00:05:31.488
No!

00:05:31.488 --> 00:05:32.750
That's crazy!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.583
I'm perfect for it.

00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:35.620
What do you mean no?

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:36.950
What?

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.993
They think I have an eating disorder?

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:40.890
No, I'm fine.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:41.723
I eat, I'm just,

00:05:41.723 --> 00:05:45.710
I totally am right for
that par-- oh, forget it.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:46.620
Ugh.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:47.453
Ah.

00:05:49.588 --> 00:05:50.470
No, it's not right.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.143
I'm calling back.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.430
You got, get me a mirror.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.436
What do you mean no?

00:05:58.436 --> 00:05:59.269
Oh.

00:05:59.269 --> 00:06:01.018
I'm calling again.

00:06:01.018 --> 00:06:02.320
How about one of these characters from

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.950
the Star Wars episodes?

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:05.300
Great, an actual Star Wars character.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.520
Yep.
Cool, let's do that.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.930
Oh cool, C-3PO.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.420
Even I know C-3PO.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.933
Rockettes C-3PO.

00:06:14.241 --> 00:06:15.880
Is there a Star Wars film,

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:16.713
I haven't seen them all,

00:06:16.713 --> 00:06:21.440
where C-3PO turns into a real badass?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.193
No, I haven't seen that yet.

00:06:23.193 --> 00:06:25.293
This is herniated disc C-3PO right here.

00:06:30.011 --> 00:06:31.630
Too many martini C-3PO.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:42.450
I'm okay.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.670
Chewbacca's saying, you are right man,

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.630
you really,

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:45.470
you had a lot to drink.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:46.694
No!

00:06:46.694 --> 00:06:47.900
I'm okay.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.900
I'm okay.

00:06:52.926 --> 00:06:55.718
(vomiting sound)

00:06:55.718 --> 00:06:58.553
(coughing)

00:06:58.553 --> 00:06:59.420
Let's put me on my set.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.480
Let's see what that looks like.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.473
Do C-3PO on your set.

00:07:02.473 --> 00:07:05.276
(drumming music)

00:07:05.276 --> 00:07:09.359
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.653
(drum beat)

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.360
You IML people are fantastic.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.760
I thank you.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.306
But before I leave this incredible place

00:07:23.306 --> 00:07:25.710
there's something I must do.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.543
Excuse me.

00:07:26.543 --> 00:07:30.136
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:07:32.653 --> 00:07:33.530
Kevin.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:34.410
Charles.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.630
Come with me.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.253
We're going outside.

00:07:52.204 --> 00:07:56.287
(audience cheering and clapping)

